{"name":"Lazy Day","hex":"#95aed1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lazy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unwilling to do work or make an effort; disinclined to exertion.","Causing or characterised by idleness; relaxed or leisurely."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To laze, act in a lazy manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lazy"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lazy Days (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lazy Days is a 1929 Our Gang short comedy film, the 89th in the series, directed by Robert F. McGowan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Lazy_days_TITLE.JPEG/330px-Lazy_days_TITLE.JPEG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lazy_Days_(film)","wikidata":"Q6506113"},{"title":"Lazy Day (Spanky and Our Gang song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lazy Day\" is a song written by Tony Powers (lyrics) and George Fischoff (music), and recorded by the 1960s band Spanky and Our Gang. It appeared on their album Spanky and Our Gang."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/Lazy_Day_-_Spanky_%26_Our_Gang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lazy_Day_(Spanky_and_Our_Gang_song)","wikidata":"Q6506110"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many